.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt POWERSTAR 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm powerstar
.Nd system tray power manager for OpenBSD
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl \-version | \-man | \-install\-man
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
puts a battery icon in the system tray of an X session and gives one
place to see and change every power setting that
.Ox
exposes through
.Xr apm 8 ,
.Xr apmd 8 ,
.Xr sysctl 8 ,
.Xr xbacklight 1
and
.Xr xset 1 .
Settings that need root are saved where
.Ox
keeps them, so they survive a reboot.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl \-version
Print the version and exit.
.It Fl \-man
Show this manual page with
.Xr man 1
without installing it.
.It Fl \-install\-man
Copy this page to
.Pa /usr/local/man/man1
and run
.Xr makewhatis 8 ,
using
.Xr doas 1 .
.El
.Pp
With no option,
.Nm
starts in the tray.
.Ss Tray icon
The icon shows the charge level, a lightning bolt while charging and a
plug while on external power without charging.
It turns orange below 30% and red at 10% or less.
Hovering shows the percentage, the status and the time left (or the time
until full while charging), as reported by
.Xr apm 8 .
A notification is shown once when the battery drops to the low level set
under General.
Clicking the icon opens Preferences.
.Ss Menu
The right-click menu shows the status, the health and cycle count of each
battery, the CPU speed, temperature and fan, and the current performance
mode.
The Performance submenu switches between Automatic, High performance and
Power saving with
.Ic apm Fl A ,
.Fl H
and
.Fl L .
This needs no password, but it lasts only until the next reboot;
.Nm
re-applies the last choice each time it starts.
The permanent default is set in Preferences.
The submenu is disabled when
.Xr apmd 8
is not running or
.Pa /var/run/apmdev
is not accessible (it is open to the wheel group).
Suspend and Hibernate run
.Xr zzz 8
and
.Xr ZZZ 8 .
.Ss Preferences
Controls the machine does not support are disabled with a reason.
Changes in the Battery, Performance and Sleep & buttons tabs need root:
Apply lists the files and commands first, then applies the values now and
saves them for boot.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Battery
Charge mode, start and stop thresholds:
.Va hw.battery.chargemode ,
.Va hw.battery.chargestart ,
.Va hw.battery.chargestop .
Per battery, refreshed live: model, charge (remaining against last full
capacity), health (last full capacity against design capacity),
discharge cycles, rate and voltage from
.Va hw.sensors .
.It Performance
Policy on external power and on battery,
.Va hw.perfpolicy
(for example
.Dq high,auto ) ;
CPU speed in manual mode,
.Va hw.setperf ;
and the CPU types the scheduler avoids,
.Va hw.blockcpu :
hyper-threads (S) and, where the machine has them, performance (P),
efficiency (E) and low-power (L) cores.
A choice that would block every core type is refused, since it leaves one
CPU running.
.It Display
Brightness with
.Xr xbacklight 1
and turning the screen off after a number of minutes with
.Xr xset 1
DPMS.
These belong to the X session, so they are stored in the user's
configuration and applied each time
.Nm
starts.
.It Sleep & buttons
What closing the lid and pressing the power button do,
.Va machdep.lidaction
and
.Va machdep.pwraction
(see
.Xr acpibtn 4 ) ,
and automatic suspend or hibernate at a battery percentage
.Pq Xr apmd 8 Fl z No and Fl Z .
Powering off from the button also needs
.Va hw.allowpowerdown=1 ,
which can only change at boot, so that choice takes effect after a reboot.
.It General
Show the percentage on the icon, the low battery notification and its
level, and how often the status is read.
.El
.Ss How settings are saved
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Xr sysctl 8
values are set now and written to
.Pa /etc/sysctl.conf .
Only the line for the changed key is replaced; a new key is appended below
a
.Dq # added by powerstar
comment.
Every other line is kept as it was.
.It
.Va hw.smt
is a deprecated alias of the S letter of
.Va hw.blockcpu .
When the CPU types are saved, an
.Va hw.smt
line is commented out with
.Dq # disabled by powerstar:
so the two lines do not fight at boot.
.It
.Xr apmd 8
flags are changed with
.Xr rcctl 8 .
Saving a performance policy removes
.Fl A ,
.Fl H
or
.Fl L
from the flags, because they would override
.Va hw.perfpolicy
when apmd starts.
.It
If any step fails, the files are restored and the values already changed
are set back.
.El
.Sh AUTHORISATION
.Nm
never asks for, sees or stores a password.
For each Apply it writes one shell script and runs it as root, trying in
order:
.Bl -enum
.It
.Ic doas Fl n ,
which works without a prompt only if
.Xr doas.conf 5
allows it.
.It
.Xr pkexec 1 ,
when polkit is installed and the desktop runs a polkit agent, which shows
its own password dialog.
.It
An
.Xr xterm 1
running
.Xr doas 1 ,
so the password goes into doas's own prompt.
.El
.Pp
Because the script is run with
.Xr sh 1 ,
the only
.Xr doas.conf 5
rule that removes the prompt is
.Dl permit nopass <user> cmd sh
which gives that user password-free root.
It works, but it is not recommended.
.Pp
The
.Ic doas persist
option does not help: it is tied to a terminal, and each Apply gets a new
one.
.Sh STARTING AT LOGIN
For
.Xr i3 1 ,
add to
.Pa ~/.config/i3/config :
.Dl exec --no-startup-id powerstar
For a plain X session, add to
.Pa ~/.xsession
before the window manager starts:
.Dl powerstar &
For Xfce, add it under Session and Startup, Application Autostart.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa ~/.config/powerstar/config.toml
brightness, screen off time, the last menu performance mode and the
General options
.It Pa /etc/sysctl.conf
saved
.Xr sysctl 8
values
.It Pa /etc/rc.conf.local
.Xr apmd 8
flags, written by
.Xr rcctl 8
.El
.Sh UNINSTALL
.Dl pipx uninstall powerstar
.Dl doas rm /usr/local/man/man1/powerstar.1
.Dl doas makewhatis /usr/local/man
Settings saved in
.Pa /etc/sysctl.conf
and the apmd flags stay; edit them by hand to undo them.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr doas 1 ,
.Xr pkexec 1 ,
.Xr xbacklight 1 ,
.Xr xset 1 ,
.Xr xterm 1 ,
.Xr acpibtn 4 ,
.Xr doas.conf 5 ,
.Xr apm 8 ,
.Xr apmd 8 ,
.Xr rcctl 8 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
